 "title": "Noise-propagation gains for B6, keyed by model id and transfer",
 "description": "Implied SD of a collagen reading (wt%) = sqrt(sum over terms of (gain x N2(window_nm))^2), N2 on the AS-MEASURED scan. Pick the entry by the model id and the transfer key actually applied to the scan before the model ('none' = no transfer, e.g. a standard-res scan, or a model valid on the scan's class as measured; otherwise the sha256 of the transfer FILE). A consensus model's SD = factor x median of its components' SDs (each component looked up with the same transfer key). No matching key: B6 is 'not assessed: no noise gains for this transfer'. Provisional: never calibrated on same-spot repeats; B6 raises a Check only. Band readability gains live in bands.json.",
 "n2": {
  "definition": "canonical N2 (reference/spyder_ref/n2.py): A = log10(1/max(R, 1e-4)) on the full as-measured grid; second difference centred on each channel; centres lo <= lambda < hi; 1.4826 x MAD; units 1e-5",
  "measured_on": "the AS-MEASURED scan, never the transferred stream"
 },
