 "provenance": {
  "method": "detector-local correlated noise (white noise in absorbance smoothed by a 1.25 nm Gaussian, matching the files' own residual autocorrelation) propagated exactly through each output's linear kernel on absorbance; transfers enter as blur (sigma 3.3973 nm, ceil(4 sigma)) x the detector's absorbance gain, linearised. Each detector's part of a kernel uses that detector's own N2 window (independent noise).",
  "checks": "Monte Carlo through the engine (transfer v0.2 + model chain): Ryder 2045 ratio 1.015; bands 1.000-1.001. Standard and v0.1 gains reproduce the Phase 0a values (Ryder 0.006102 / 0.003326; OH-corrected 2045 0.019809 / 0.009504; OH-corrected 1500 0.030097 / 0.015714). Earlier N-H set (F05) gains (0.008748 / 0.004337 standard) came from a least-squares split of Monte Carlo SDs between two collinear windows; the per-detector analytic gains here give the same total SD within ~10% on standard and noisy high-res scans and are separable.",
  "data": "noise model only; checked against within-bone scatter of a high-res variation set (statistics only)"
 },
